      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A double-blind, between-patients trial of a new drug (parsalmide) against indomethacin in the relief of inflammation and pain in 68 patients with exacerbated inflammatory and-or degenerative arthromyopathy resulted in 76% of successful results with both drugs. Tolerance was good, though side-effects, albeit slight, were more common with indomethacin."},
